-- Income Tax Ordinance [New Version], s 91: the tax on a capital gain.
-- Quotations (`src:N`) are copied mechanically from line N of
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/income-tax-ordinance-new-version.he.wiki.txt (sha256 b87f2cf4...6b81b6).
--
-- WHAT IT SAYS.
--  (a)  A body of persons pays tax on a real capital gain at the rate of s 126(a).
--  (b)  (1) An individual pays tax on a real capital gain as in s 121, at a rate not above 25%, the gain being regarded as the highest layer of
--       the taxable income. (2) On the sale of a security in a body of persons in which the seller, an individual, was a material shareholder
--       at the sale or at some time in the twelve months before it, the rate does not exceed 30%. (3) On the sale of a bond, commercial
--       security, loan note or loan that is not linked to the index, the rate does not exceed 15%, or 20% for a material shareholder, and the whole
--       gain is regarded as real gain.
--  (b1) For an asset whose purchase day is before the change date (1 January 2012), other than unpaid-for goodwill: (1)(a) an asset bought before
--       the fixed date (1 January 2003): the real gain up to the fixed date at the rate of s 121, the real gain from the fixed date to the change
--       date at s 121 but not above 20% (25% under (b)(2); the rate of (b)(3) under (b)(3)), the remainder at the rate of (b)(1), (2) or (3);
--       (b) an asset bought after the fixed date: the last two parts only; (1A) a security bought before the fixed date: the real gain is reduced
--       by the distributable profits of s 94B for the first and the last part; (1B) not for a security listed before the change date nor a unit in
--       an exempt mutual fund; (2) the gain is regarded as the highest layer of the taxable income.
--  (b2) A unit in an oil or film partnership: the part of the gain equal to the depletion, exploration and development deductions or film expenses is
--       taxed as in s 121 for an individual, at s 126(a) for a body of persons.
--  (c)  The tax on the chargeable inflationary amount is 10%.
--  (d)  The report and advance within 30 days: procedure, not encoded (NOTES.md coverage table).
--  (e)  At the taxpayer's request the tax on the real gain is computed as if it arose in equal annual parts over the shorter of four tax years and
--       the period of ownership, ending in the tax year of the gain; not for exchange-listed securities; the rates of (b), the rates on the total
--       taxable income of each year and the credit points left that year being taken into account.
--  (f)  An asset acquired up to tax year 1948: the tax does not exceed 12% of the capital gain; acquired 1949 to 1960: 12% plus 1% for each year
--       from 1949 to the year of acquisition; from tax year 2005 add 1% for each tax year or part; but if that rate exceeds the rate of (a) or
--       (b)(1) or (2), the gain is taxed at those rates.
--  (g)  On expropriation the tax is half the tax under (a) to (f).
--  (h)  The power to fix rates for transfers between controlling shareholders and connected parties: not encoded (a power, no rule in the text).
--
-- WHAT IS AN INPUT. The real capital gain, the capital gain, the chargeable inflationary amount, the purchase and sale days come from s 88
-- (ito-88-definitions.l4 computes them from a sale record); the s 126(a) rate (s 126 is not encoded); the distributable profits of s 94B (s 94B is
-- not encoded); the individual's other taxable income and the scale of s 121 (row IL-03) and, for (e), the credit points left unused each year.
--
-- WHICH SALES IT ANSWERS: from the change date (1 January 2012). The text before the amendments of the 5772 round is not deposited, so an
-- earlier sale is declined (NOTES.md, assumption A6; needs a source).
--
-- THE FORKS (NOTES.md fork register). T3 (0.1.1, a period of ownership that is empty), S1/S4 (material shareholder), S2 (counting the days), T1 (a cap where the gain stands in several bands), T2
-- (where each part stands in the top layer), D2 (the time the shareholding is tested in (b)(3)), V1, V2 (the years counted in (f)) and V3 (the
-- real gain for the middle part of (b1)(1A)). Each declines by default where the readings give different answers.

§ `Section 91 — the tax on a capital gain`

§§ `The refusals of section 91`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`section 91 as deposited states the rates for a sale from the change date on` MEANS
    REFUSE "the deposited text of section 91 is the text as amended to 2017, and the text for a sale before the change date, 1 January 2012, is not deposited"

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax turns on a reading that section 91 or section 88 leaves open` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 91 or section 88 leaves open a reading (the layer, the cap, the days of a period, who is a material shareholder, or the years of paragraph (f)), and here the tax turns on it"

GIVETH A NUMBER
`section 91(b2) for an individual leaves the place of the taxed part in the scale unsaid` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 91(b2) taxes the part of an individual's gain equal to depletion deductions as in section 121, and does not say where that part stands in the scale"

GIVETH A NUMBER
`section 91(b1)(1A) leaves the parts of the reduced gain unsaid and here they part` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 91(b1)(1A) reduces the real gain by the distributable profits for the first and the last part, and the text does not say whether the middle part is reduced; here it changes the answer"

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the parts of a gain bought before the fixed date do not add up under this reading of section 91(b1)(1A)` MEANS
    REFUSE "the parts of the gain do not add up under the reading of section 91(b1)(1A) that leaves the middle part unreduced: the last part would be negative"

§§ `The caps of (b), (b1) and (b)(3)`

-- src:3346 | (א) חבר־בני־אדם יהיה חייב במס על רווח הון ריאלי בשיעור הקבוע בסעיף 126(א).
-- src:3347 | (ב)(1) יחיד יהיה חייב במס על רווח הון ריאלי כאמור בסעיף 121, בשיעור שלא יעלה על 25%, ויראו את רווח ההון כשלב הגבוה ביותר בסולם הכנסתו החייבת.
-- src:3348 | (2) על אף האמור בפסקה (1), רווח הון ריאלי כאמור בסעיף 121, במכירת נייר ערך בחבר־בני־אדם שבו המוכר הוא יחיד שהוא בעל מניות מהותי במועד מכירתו של נייר הערך או במועד כלשהו ב־12 החודשים שקדמו למכירה, יחויב במס בשיעור שלא יעלה על 30%.
-- src:3349 | (3)(א) על אף האמור בפסקאות (1) ו־(2), רווח הון במכירת איגרת חוב, נייר ערך מסחרי, מילווה או הלוואה, שאינם צמודים למדד, יחויב במס בשיעור שלא יעלה על 15%, או של 20% לענין בעל מניות מהותי, ויראו את כל רווח ההון כרווח הון ריאלי.
-- src:3350 | (ב) שר האוצר רשאי לשנות בצו את שיעור המס הקבוע בפסקת משנה (א), בהתאם לשינוי במדד.
-- src:3351 | (ג) לענין פסקה זו, ”אינם צמודים למדד“ – ערכם הנקוב או סכומם אינו צמוד למדד, או שהוא צמוד בחלקו לשיעור עליית המדד, כולו או חלקו, והכל עד לפדיון או להחזר.

-- The highest rate for a gain taxed under (b): 25%; 30% for a security in a body of persons sold by a material shareholder; 15%, or 20%
-- for a material shareholder, for a bond and the like that is not linked to the index.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 91(b)(1)-(3) (source lines 3347-3351)
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `The kind of asset sold, for section 91`
      m          IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 91(b) — the highest rate for` `the kind` `when the seller is a material shareholder:` m MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `a security in a body of persons`                                                   THEN IF m THEN 30% ELSE 25%
    WHEN `a bond, commercial security, loan note or loan that is not linked to the index`    THEN IF m THEN 20% ELSE 15%
    WHEN `goodwill that was not paid for`                                                    THEN 25%
    WHEN `any other asset`                                                                   THEN 25%

-- src:3352 | (ב1)(1) על אף הוראות סעיף קטן (ב), לגבי נכס שיום רכישתו חל לפני מועד השינוי, למעט נכס שהוא מוניטין שלא שולם בעד רכישתו, יחולו הוראות אלה:
-- src:3353 | (א) נרכש הנכס לפני המועד הקובע, יחויב רווח ההון הריאלי במס בשיעורים כמפורט להלן:
-- src:3354 | (1) על רווח ההון הריאלי עד המועד הקובע – כאמור בסעיף 121;
-- src:3355 | (2) על רווח ההון הריאלי לאחר המועד הקובע ועד למועד השינוי – כאמור בסעיף 121 בשיעור שלא יעלה על 20%, ואולם אם מתקיים האמור בסעיף קטן (ב)(2) – בשיעור שלא יעלה על 25%, ובהתקיים האמור בסעיף קטן (ב)(3) – בשיעור הקבוע באותו סעיף קטן;
-- src:3356 | (3) על יתרת רווח ההון הריאלי לאחר מועד השינוי – בשיעור הקבוע בסעיף קטן (ב)(1), (2) או (3), לפי העניין;
-- src:3357 | (ב) נרכש הנכס לאחר המועד הקובע, יחויבו רווח ההון הריאלי לאחר המועד הקובע ועד למועד השינוי ויתרת רווח ההון הריאלי לאחר מועד השינוי, במס, בהתאם להוראות פסקת משנה (א)(2) ו־(3).
-- src:3358 | (1א) במכירת נייר ערך שיום רכישתו לפני המועד הקובע, לענין חישוב רווח ההון הריאלי שעד המועד הקובע ולענין יתרת רווח ההון, יראו את רווח ההון הריאלי כרווח ההון הריאלי לאחר שהופחתו ממנו הרווחים הראויים לחלוקה שחושבו כאמור בסעיף 94ב.
-- (b1)(1)(a)(2): the real gain after the fixed date up to the change date: s 121, but not above 20%; 25% if (b)(2) holds; the rate of (b)(3) if (b)(3) holds.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 91(b1)(1)(a)(2) (source line 3355)
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `The kind of asset sold, for section 91`
      m          IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 91(b1) — the highest rate for the middle period for` `the kind` `when the seller is a material shareholder:` m MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `a security in a body of persons`                                                   THEN IF m THEN 25% ELSE 20%
    WHEN `a bond, commercial security, loan note or loan that is not linked to the index`    THEN IF m THEN 20% ELSE 15%
    WHEN `goodwill that was not paid for`                                                    THEN 20%
    WHEN `any other asset`                                                                   THEN 20%

-- Fork D2 and forks S1, S4: is the individual a material shareholder in the body concerned, for (b)(2) and (b)(3)?
-- (b)(2) names the time (at the sale or in the twelve months before it); (b)(3) names none.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 91(b)(2), (b)(3) (source lines 3348-3349); forks S1, S4, D2
GIVEN `the sale` IS A `A sale for section 91`
      r          IS A `The readings of the forks in sections 88, 91, 125B and 125C`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 91 — whether the seller is a material shareholder, for` `the sale` `, reading the forks as` r MEANS
    CONSIDER `the sale`'s `the seller`
    WHEN `a body of persons` `the rate`                                                             THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an individual` `the records`
      THEN CONSIDER `the sale`'s `the kind of asset sold`
           WHEN `a security in a body of persons`
             THEN `over the twelve months` `the records`
           WHEN `a bond, commercial security, loan note or loan that is not linked to the index`
             THEN `s 88 — whether a material shareholder on a recorded day from any of` `the first days` `up to` (`the sale`'s `the sale day`) `, by the records` `the records` `, reading together with another as` (r's `together with another`)
           WHEN `goodwill that was not paid for`   THEN JUST FALSE
           WHEN `any other asset`                  THEN JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `the first days` MEANS
            CONSIDER r's `the time of the test in section 91(b)(3)`
            WHEN `at the time of the sale only`                                         THEN LIST `the sale`'s `the sale day`
            WHEN `at the time of the sale or at some time in the twelve months before it` THEN `s 88 — the candidate first days of the twelve months before` (`the sale`'s `the sale day`) `, reading them as` (r's `the twelve months before a day`)
            WHEN `at any time up to the sale`                                           THEN LIST (YMD 1900 1 1)
            WHEN `declined where the time of the sale test changes the answer`
              THEN append (LIST `the sale`'s `the sale day`) (append (`s 88 — the candidate first days of the twelve months before` (`the sale`'s `the sale day`) `, reading them as` (r's `the twelve months before a day`)) (LIST (YMD 1900 1 1)))
        `over the twelve months` MEANS
            GIVEN recs YIELD
                `s 88 — whether a material shareholder on` (`the sale`'s `the sale day`) `or at any time in the twelve months before it, by the records` recs `, reading the forks as` r

§§ `Where the layered rates of (b1) apply, and the gain taxed`

-- src:3352 | (ב1)(1) על אף הוראות סעיף קטן (ב), לגבי נכס שיום רכישתו חל לפני מועד השינוי, למעט נכס שהוא מוניטין שלא שולם בעד רכישתו, יחולו הוראות אלה:
-- src:3359 | (1ב) הוראות סעיף קטן זה לא יחולו במכירת ניירות ערך הרשומים למסחר בבורסה ושנרשמו למסחר לפני מועד השינוי וכן במכירת יחידה בקרן נאמנות פטורה, ויחולו הוראות סעיף קטן (ב)(1) או (2), לפי העניין.
-- src:3360 | (2) לענין סעיף קטן זה, יראו את רווח ההון כשלב הגבוה ביותר בסולם ההכנסה החייבת.
-- src:3361 | (ב2) על אף הוראות סעיפים קטנים (א), (ב) ו־(ב1), במכירת יחידת השתתפות בשותפות נפט ובמכירת יחידת השתתפות בשותפות סרטים, חלק רווח ההון הריאלי בגובה ניכוי אזילה, בגובה ניכוי הוצאות חיפוש ופיתוח או בגובה הוצאות הפקת סרט, שהותרו בתקנות לפי סעיפים 20, 31 ו־98, לפי הענין, יחויב במס כאמור בסעיף 121 – לגבי יחיד, ובשיעור הקבוע בסעיף 126(א) – לגבי חבר־בני־אדם.
-- src:3362 | (ג) המס על הסכום האינפלציוני החייב יהיה 10%.

-- (b1) applies to an individual's asset whose purchase day is before the change date, other than unpaid-for goodwill, and (1B) takes out
-- a security listed on the stock exchange before the change date and a unit in an exempt mutual fund.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 91(b1)(1), (1B) (source lines 3352, 3359)
GIVEN `the sale` IS A `A sale for section 91`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 91(b1) — the layered rates apply to` `the sale` MEANS
        `the seller is an individual`
    AND `the sale`'s `the purchase day` LESS THAN `s 88 — the change date`
    AND NOT `the asset is unpaid-for goodwill`
    AND NOT `paragraph (1B) takes it out`
    WHERE
        `the seller is an individual` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the sale`'s `the seller`
            WHEN `an individual` `the records`   THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a body of persons` `the rate`  THEN FALSE
        `the asset is unpaid-for goodwill` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the sale`'s `the kind of asset sold`
            WHEN `a security in a body of persons`                                                  THEN FALSE
            WHEN `a bond, commercial security, loan note or loan that is not linked to the index`   THEN FALSE
            WHEN `goodwill that was not paid for`                                                   THEN TRUE
            WHEN `any other asset`                                                                  THEN FALSE
        `paragraph (1B) takes it out` MEANS
                (   `the sale`'s `registered for trading on a stock exchange`
                AND `the sale`'s `registered for trading on a stock exchange before the change date`)
             OR `the sale`'s `a unit in an exempt mutual fund`

-- (b)(3): the whole gain is regarded as real gain; otherwise the real capital gain of s 88.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 91(b)(3) (source line 3349); assumption A10
GIVEN `the sale` IS A `A sale for section 91`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 91 — the real capital gain to be taxed, of` `the sale` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the sale`'s `the kind of asset sold`
    WHEN `a security in a body of persons`                                                  THEN `the sale`'s `the real capital gain`
    WHEN `a bond, commercial security, loan note or loan that is not linked to the index`   THEN `the sale`'s `the capital gain`
    WHEN `goodwill that was not paid for`                                                   THEN `the sale`'s `the real capital gain`
    WHEN `any other asset`                                                                  THEN `the sale`'s `the real capital gain`

-- (c): the tax on the chargeable inflationary amount is 10%. Where the whole gain is regarded as real gain, (b)(3), there is no inflationary
-- amount and so nothing chargeable (assumption A10).
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 91(c) (source line 3362); assumption A10
GIVEN `the sale` IS A `A sale for section 91`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 91(c) — the tax on the chargeable inflationary amount of` `the sale` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the sale`'s `the kind of asset sold`
    WHEN `a security in a body of persons`                                                  THEN `the sale`'s `the chargeable inflationary amount` TIMES 10%
    WHEN `a bond, commercial security, loan note or loan that is not linked to the index`   THEN 0
    WHEN `goodwill that was not paid for`                                                   THEN `the sale`'s `the chargeable inflationary amount` TIMES 10%
    WHEN `any other asset`                                                                  THEN `the sale`'s `the chargeable inflationary amount` TIMES 10%

§§ `The tax of an individual on the real gain, at explicit readings`

-- (b): the gain is a layer on top of the other taxable income, at a rate not above the cap.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 91(b)(1)-(3) (source lines 3347-3351); fork T1
GIVEN `the sale` IS A `A sale for section 91`
      m          IS A BOOLEAN
      t          IS A `A reading of a cap on the rate where the gain stands in several bands`
      a          IS A NUMBER
      bands      IS A LIST OF `A band of a marginal scale`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 91(b) — the tax of an individual on the real gain of` `the sale` `, a material shareholder:` m `, applying the cap as` t `, above the other taxable income` a `under the scale` bands MEANS
    `the tax on a layer of` (`s 91 — the real capital gain to be taxed, of` `the sale`) `standing on the other taxable income` a `under the scale` bands `with the rate capped at` (`s 91(b) — the highest rate for` (`the sale`'s `the kind of asset sold`) `when the seller is a material shareholder:` m) `, applying the cap as` t

-- (b1)(1) and (2): the gain in three parts, each with its own cap, standing in the top layer in the order fork T2 names.
-- The parts: up to the fixed date, from it to the change date, and the remainder (s 88). (1A): for a security bought before the fixed date the
-- real gain, for the first part and the remainder, is the real gain less the distributable profits of s 94B (fork V3 for the middle part).
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 91(b1)(1)-(2), (1A) (source lines 3352-3360); s 88 (lines 3311-3314); forks S2, T1, T2, V3
GIVEN `the sale` IS A `A sale for section 91`
      m          IS A BOOLEAN
      c          IS A `A reading of how the days of a period are counted`
      t          IS A `A reading of a cap on the rate where the gain stands in several bands`
      o          IS A `A reading of where each part of a gain stands in the top layer`
      v          IS A `A reading of the real gain used for the middle part of a security bought before the fixed date`
      a          IS A NUMBER
      bands      IS A LIST OF `A band of a marginal scale`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 91(b1) — the tax of an individual on the real gain of` `the sale` `, a material shareholder:` m `, counting the days as` c `, applying the cap as` t `, placing the parts as` o `, reading the middle part of a security as` v `, above the other taxable income` a `under the scale` bands MEANS
    IF   `the last part` LESS THAN 0
    THEN `the parts of a gain bought before the fixed date do not add up under this reading of section 91(b1)(1A)`
    ELSE `the tax of three parts` `the first part` `and` `the middle part` `and` `the last part` `capped at` `these rates are percentages, and nothing in the scale exceeds a hundred percent` `and` `the cap of the middle part` `and` `the cap of the last part` `above the other taxable income` a `under the scale` bands `, applying the cap as` t `, with the parts placed as` o
    WHERE
        `the gain` MEANS `s 91 — the real capital gain to be taxed, of` `the sale`
        `the reduction applies` MEANS
                `the sale`'s `the asset is a security`
            AND `the sale`'s `the purchase day` LESS THAN `s 88 — the fixed date`
            AND `the sale`'s `the distributable profits of section 94B deducted for a security bought before the fixed date` GREATER THAN 0
        `the reduced gain` MEANS max 0 (`the gain` MINUS `the sale`'s `the distributable profits of section 94B deducted for a security bought before the fixed date`)
        `the gain for the first and the last part` MEANS IF `the reduction applies` THEN `the reduced gain` ELSE `the gain`
        `the gain for the middle part` MEANS
            IF `the reduction applies`
            THEN CONSIDER v
                 WHEN `the gain reduced by the distributable profits is used for all three parts`  THEN `the reduced gain`
                 WHEN `the gain before the reduction is used for the middle part`                  THEN `the gain`
                 WHEN `declined where the real gain used for the middle part changes the answer`   THEN `the reduced gain`
            ELSE `the gain`
        `the first part` MEANS
            `s 88 — the real capital gain up to the fixed date, of` `the gain for the first and the last part` `bought on` (`the sale`'s `the purchase day`) `and sold on` (`the sale`'s `the sale day`) `, counting the days as` c
        `the middle part` MEANS
            `s 88 — the real capital gain after the fixed date up to the change date, of` `the gain for the middle part` `bought on` (`the sale`'s `the purchase day`) `and sold on` (`the sale`'s `the sale day`) `, counting the days as` c
        `the last part` MEANS `the gain for the first and the last part` MINUS `the first part` MINUS `the middle part`
        `the cap of the middle part` MEANS `s 91(b1) — the highest rate for the middle period for` (`the sale`'s `the kind of asset sold`) `when the seller is a material shareholder:` m
        `the cap of the last part` MEANS `s 91(b) — the highest rate for` (`the sale`'s `the kind of asset sold`) `when the seller is a material shareholder:` m

§§ `Paragraph (f): old assets`

-- src:3387 | (ו)(1) לגבי נכס שנרכש עד שנת המס 1948 לא יעלה המס על 12% מריווח ההון, ולגבי נכס שנרכש בשנות המס 1949 עד 1960 לא יעלה המס על 12% מריווח ההון ועוד 1% לכל שנה משנת המס 1949 ועד לשנת הרכישה.
-- src:3388 | (2) החל בשנת המס 2005, ייווסף לשיעור המס על פי פסקת משנה (1), 1% לכל שנת מס, או חלק ממנה, ואולם אם שיעור המס על רווח ההון בשנת המכירה לפי הוראות סעיף קטן זה עולה על השיעור הקבוע בסעיפים קטנים (א) או (ב)(1) או (2), לפי הענין, יחויב רווח ההון בשיעורים לפי הוראות סעיפים קטנים (א) או (ב)(1) או (2), לפי הענין.

GIVEN r IS A `A reading of the years counted from 1949 in section 91(f)(1)`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A reading of the years counted from 1949 in section 91(f)(1)`
`s 91(f) — the explicit readings of the years from 1949 in` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `1949 and the year of acquisition are both counted`           THEN LIST `1949 and the year of acquisition are both counted`
    WHEN `1949 is counted and the year of acquisition is not`          THEN LIST `1949 is counted and the year of acquisition is not`
    WHEN `declined where the number of years changes the answer`
      THEN LIST `1949 and the year of acquisition are both counted`, `1949 is counted and the year of acquisition is not`

GIVEN r IS A `A reading of the years counted from 2005 in section 91(f)(2)`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A reading of the years counted from 2005 in section 91(f)(2)`
`s 91(f) — the explicit readings of the years from 2005 in` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `2005 and the tax year of the sale are both counted`                       THEN LIST `2005 and the tax year of the sale are both counted`
    WHEN `2005 is not counted: the years after it up to the tax year of the sale`   THEN LIST `2005 is not counted: the years after it up to the tax year of the sale`
    WHEN `declined where the number of years changes the answer`
      THEN LIST `2005 and the tax year of the sale are both counted`, `2005 is not counted: the years after it up to the tax year of the sale`

-- The rate of paragraph (f), at explicit readings of V1 and V2: NOTHING if the asset was acquired after tax year 1960 (the paragraph says
-- nothing of it).
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 91(f)(1)-(2) (source lines 3387-3388); forks V1, V2
GIVEN `the sale` IS A `A sale for section 91`
      v1         IS A `A reading of the years counted from 1949 in section 91(f)(1)`
      v2         IS A `A reading of the years counted from 2005 in section 91(f)(2)`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 91(f) — the rate for` `the sale` `, counting the years from 1949 as` v1 `and from 2005 as` v2 MEANS
    IF   `the year of acquisition` GREATER THAN 1960
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the rate before 2005` PLUS 1% TIMES `the years from 2005`)
    WHERE
        `the year of acquisition` MEANS `the sale`'s `the tax year in which the asset reached the seller`
        `the sale year` MEANS DATE_YEAR (`the sale`'s `the sale day`)
        `the years from 1949` MEANS
            CONSIDER v1
            WHEN `1949 and the year of acquisition are both counted`      THEN `the year of acquisition` MINUS 1948
            WHEN `1949 is counted and the year of acquisition is not`     THEN `the year of acquisition` MINUS 1949
            WHEN `declined where the number of years changes the answer`  THEN `the year of acquisition` MINUS 1948
        `the rate before 2005` MEANS
            IF `the year of acquisition` AT MOST 1948 THEN 12% ELSE 12% PLUS 1% TIMES `the years from 1949`
        `the years from 2005` MEANS
            IF   `the sale year` LESS THAN 2005
            THEN 0
            ELSE CONSIDER v2
                 WHEN `2005 and the tax year of the sale are both counted`                       THEN `the sale year` MINUS 2004
                 WHEN `2005 is not counted: the years after it up to the tax year of the sale`   THEN `the sale year` MINUS 2005
                 WHEN `declined where the number of years changes the answer`                    THEN `the sale year` MINUS 2004

-- All the paragraph (f) rates over the readings left open: empty if the paragraph does not reach the asset.
GIVEN `the sale` IS A `A sale for section 91`
      r          IS A `The readings of the forks in sections 88, 91, 125B and 125C`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`s 91(f) — the rates for` `the sale` `at every reading left open, reading the forks as` r MEANS
    concat (map (GIVEN v1 YIELD
                    map (GIVEN v2 YIELD
                            CONSIDER `s 91(f) — the rate for` `the sale` `, counting the years from 1949 as` v1 `and from 2005 as` v2
                            WHEN JUST x  THEN x
                            WHEN NOTHING THEN 0 MINUS 1)
                        (`s 91(f) — the explicit readings of the years from 2005 in` (r's `the years from 2005 in section 91(f)(2)`)))
                (`s 91(f) — the explicit readings of the years from 1949 in` (r's `the years from 1949 in section 91(f)(1)`)))

-- (f)(1)-(2), applied to a total: if the (f) rate exceeds the ordinary highest rate, the ordinary rates; else the tax does not exceed the (f) rate of the capital gain.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 91(f)(1)-(2) (source lines 3387-3388)
GIVEN `the ordinary tax`    IS A NUMBER
      `the rate of (f)`     IS A NUMBER
      `the capital gain`    IS A NUMBER
      `the ordinary highest rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 91(f) — the tax` `the ordinary tax` `where the rate of (f) is` `the rate of (f)` `on a capital gain of` `the capital gain` `and the ordinary highest rate is` `the ordinary highest rate` MEANS
    IF   `the rate of (f)` GREATER THAN `the ordinary highest rate`
    THEN `the ordinary tax`
    ELSE min `the ordinary tax` (`the rate of (f)` TIMES `the capital gain`)

§§ `Paragraph (g): expropriation`

-- src:3389 | (ז) המס שיחול על ריווח הון בהפקעת נכס הוא מחצית המס המתחייב על פי סעיפים קטנים (א) עד (ו).
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 91(g) (source line 3389)
GIVEN x      IS A NUMBER
      `taken` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 91(g) — the tax` x `if the asset was expropriated:` `taken` MEANS
    IF `taken` THEN x DIVIDED BY 2 ELSE x

§§ `The totals of a sale, at every reading left open`

-- The totals for a body of persons: the real gain at the rate of s 126(a), plus the tax on the chargeable inflationary amount, then (f) and (g).
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 91(a), (c), (f), (g) (source lines 3346, 3362, 3387-3389)
GIVEN `the sale` IS A `A sale for section 91`
      `the rate`  IS A NUMBER
      r           IS A `The readings of the forks in sections 88, 91, 125B and 125C`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`s 91 — the totals for a body of persons for` `the sale` `at the rate` `the rate` `, reading the forks as` r MEANS
    map (GIVEN x YIELD `s 91(g) — the tax` x `if the asset was expropriated:` (`the sale`'s `the asset was expropriated`))
        (IF   null `the (f) rates`
         THEN LIST `the ordinary tax`
         ELSE map (GIVEN fr YIELD `s 91(f) — the tax` `the ordinary tax` `where the rate of (f) is` fr `on a capital gain of` (`the sale`'s `the capital gain`) `and the ordinary highest rate is` `the rate`) `the (f) rates`)
    WHERE
        `the ordinary tax` MEANS
            `s 91 — the real capital gain to be taxed, of` `the sale` TIMES `the rate` PLUS `s 91(c) — the tax on the chargeable inflationary amount of` `the sale`
        `the (f) rates` MEANS filter (GIVEN x YIELD x AT LEAST 0) (`s 91(f) — the rates for` `the sale` `at every reading left open, reading the forks as` r)

-- The explicit readings of fork V3.
GIVEN r IS A `A reading of the real gain used for the middle part of a security bought before the fixed date`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A reading of the real gain used for the middle part of a security bought before the fixed date`
`s 91(b1) — the explicit readings of the middle part in` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `the gain reduced by the distributable profits is used for all three parts`  THEN LIST `the gain reduced by the distributable profits is used for all three parts`
    WHEN `the gain before the reduction is used for the middle part`                  THEN LIST `the gain before the reduction is used for the middle part`
    WHEN `declined where the real gain used for the middle part changes the answer`
      THEN LIST `the gain reduced by the distributable profits is used for all three parts`, `the gain before the reduction is used for the middle part`

-- The ordinary taxes of an individual under (b1), one for each combination of the readings left open, with (c) added. The four readings
-- are expanded one at a time, the innermost first.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 91(b1), (c) (source lines 3352-3362); forks S2, T1, T2, V3
GIVEN `the sale` IS A `A sale for section 91`
      m          IS A BOOLEAN
      c          IS A `A reading of how the days of a period are counted`
      t          IS A `A reading of a cap on the rate where the gain stands in several bands`
      o          IS A `A reading of where each part of a gain stands in the top layer`
      a          IS A NUMBER
      bands      IS A LIST OF `A band of a marginal scale`
      r          IS A `The readings of the forks in sections 88, 91, 125B and 125C`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`s 91(b1) — the ordinary taxes for` `the sale` `, a material shareholder:` m `, days counted as` c `, cap applied as` t `, parts placed as` o `, above the other taxable income` a `under the scale` bands `, reading the forks as` r MEANS
    map (GIVEN v YIELD `the tax at v` v) (`s 91(b1) — the explicit readings of the middle part in` (r's `the real gain for the middle part`))
    WHERE
        `the tax at v` MEANS
            GIVEN v YIELD
                `s 91(b1) — the tax of an individual on the real gain of` `the sale` `, a material shareholder:` m `, counting the days as` c `, applying the cap as` t `, placing the parts as` o `, reading the middle part of a security as` v `, above the other taxable income` a `under the scale` bands
                PLUS `s 91(c) — the tax on the chargeable inflationary amount of` `the sale`

GIVEN `the sale` IS A `A sale for section 91`
      m          IS A BOOLEAN
      c          IS A `A reading of how the days of a period are counted`
      t          IS A `A reading of a cap on the rate where the gain stands in several bands`
      a          IS A NUMBER
      bands      IS A LIST OF `A band of a marginal scale`
      r          IS A `The readings of the forks in sections 88, 91, 125B and 125C`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`s 91(b1) — the ordinary taxes for` `the sale` `, a material shareholder:` m `, days counted as` c `, cap applied as` t `, above the other taxable income` a `under the scale` bands `, reading the forks as` r MEANS
    concat (map (GIVEN o YIELD `the taxes at o` o) (`the explicit readings of where the parts stand in` (r's `where each part stands in the top layer`)))
    WHERE
        `the taxes at o` MEANS
            GIVEN o YIELD
                `s 91(b1) — the ordinary taxes for` `the sale` `, a material shareholder:` m `, days counted as` c `, cap applied as` t `, parts placed as` o `, above the other taxable income` a `under the scale` bands `, reading the forks as` r

GIVEN `the sale` IS A `A sale for section 91`
      m          IS A BOOLEAN
      c          IS A `A reading of how the days of a period are counted`
      a          IS A NUMBER
      bands      IS A LIST OF `A band of a marginal scale`
      r          IS A `The readings of the forks in sections 88, 91, 125B and 125C`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`s 91(b1) — the ordinary taxes for` `the sale` `, a material shareholder:` m `, days counted as` c `, above the other taxable income` a `under the scale` bands `, reading the forks as` r MEANS
    concat (map (GIVEN t YIELD `the taxes at t` t) (`the explicit readings of the cap in` (r's `a cap where the gain stands in several bands`)))
    WHERE
        `the taxes at t` MEANS
            GIVEN t YIELD
                `s 91(b1) — the ordinary taxes for` `the sale` `, a material shareholder:` m `, days counted as` c `, cap applied as` t `, above the other taxable income` a `under the scale` bands `, reading the forks as` r

GIVEN `the sale` IS A `A sale for section 91`
      m          IS A BOOLEAN
      a          IS A NUMBER
      bands      IS A LIST OF `A band of a marginal scale`
      r          IS A `The readings of the forks in sections 88, 91, 125B and 125C`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`s 91(b1) — the ordinary taxes of an individual for` `the sale` `, a material shareholder:` m `, above the other taxable income` a `under the scale` bands `, reading the forks as` r MEANS
    concat (map (GIVEN c YIELD `the taxes at c` c) (`s 88 — the explicit readings of the day count in` (r's `counting the days of a period`)))
    WHERE
        `the taxes at c` MEANS
            GIVEN c YIELD
                `s 91(b1) — the ordinary taxes for` `the sale` `, a material shareholder:` m `, days counted as` c `, above the other taxable income` a `under the scale` bands `, reading the forks as` r

-- The ordinary taxes of an individual under (b), one for each reading of the cap left open, with (c) added.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 91(b), (c) (source lines 3347-3351, 3362); fork T1
GIVEN `the sale` IS A `A sale for section 91`
      m          IS A BOOLEAN
      a          IS A NUMBER
      bands      IS A LIST OF `A band of a marginal scale`
      r          IS A `The readings of the forks in sections 88, 91, 125B and 125C`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`s 91(b) — the ordinary taxes of an individual for` `the sale` `, a material shareholder:` m `, above the other taxable income` a `under the scale` bands `, reading the forks as` r MEANS
    map (GIVEN t YIELD
            `s 91(b) — the tax of an individual on the real gain of` `the sale` `, a material shareholder:` m `, applying the cap as` t `, above the other taxable income` a `under the scale` bands
            PLUS `s 91(c) — the tax on the chargeable inflationary amount of` `the sale`)
        (`the explicit readings of the cap in` (r's `a cap where the gain stands in several bands`))

-- The ordinary highest rate that (f)(2) compares the (f) rate with: the rate of (b)(2) for a security sold by a material shareholder, else (b)(1)'s.
GIVEN `the sale` IS A `A sale for section 91`
      m          IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 91(f)(2) — the ordinary highest rate for` `the sale` `when the seller is a material shareholder:` m MEANS
    CONSIDER `the sale`'s `the kind of asset sold`
    WHEN `a security in a body of persons`                                                  THEN IF m THEN 30% ELSE 25%
    WHEN `a bond, commercial security, loan note or loan that is not linked to the index`   THEN 25%
    WHEN `goodwill that was not paid for`                                                   THEN 25%
    WHEN `any other asset`                                                                  THEN 25%

-- The totals for one status of the shareholder: the ordinary taxes, then (f), then (g).
GIVEN `the sale` IS A `A sale for section 91`
      m          IS A BOOLEAN
      a          IS A NUMBER
      bands      IS A LIST OF `A band of a marginal scale`
      r          IS A `The readings of the forks in sections 88, 91, 125B and 125C`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`s 91 — the totals for an individual for` `the sale` `, a material shareholder:` m `, above the other taxable income` a `under the scale` bands `, reading the forks as` r MEANS
    map (GIVEN x YIELD `s 91(g) — the tax` x `if the asset was expropriated:` (`the sale`'s `the asset was expropriated`))
        (IF   null `the (f) rates`
         THEN `the ordinary taxes`
         ELSE concat (map (GIVEN ord YIELD
                              map (GIVEN fr YIELD `s 91(f) — the tax` ord `where the rate of (f) is` fr `on a capital gain of` (`the sale`'s `the capital gain`) `and the ordinary highest rate is` (`s 91(f)(2) — the ordinary highest rate for` `the sale` `when the seller is a material shareholder:` m))
                                  `the (f) rates`)
                          `the ordinary taxes`))
    WHERE
        `the (f) rates` MEANS filter (GIVEN x YIELD x AT LEAST 0) (`s 91(f) — the rates for` `the sale` `at every reading left open, reading the forks as` r)
        `the ordinary taxes` MEANS
            IF   `s 91(b1) — the layered rates apply to` `the sale`
            THEN `s 91(b1) — the ordinary taxes of an individual for` `the sale` `, a material shareholder:` m `, above the other taxable income` a `under the scale` bands `, reading the forks as` r
            ELSE `s 91(b) — the ordinary taxes of an individual for` `the sale` `, a material shareholder:` m `, above the other taxable income` a `under the scale` bands `, reading the forks as` r

-- The alternatives for the status of the material shareholder: the answer where settled, both where the readings part.
GIVEN `the status` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF BOOLEAN
`s 91 — the material shareholder alternatives` `the status` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the status`
    WHEN JUST b  THEN LIST b
    WHEN NOTHING THEN LIST TRUE, FALSE

-- The totals for an individual, over the alternatives for the status.
GIVEN `the sale` IS A `A sale for section 91`
      a          IS A NUMBER
      bands      IS A LIST OF `A band of a marginal scale`
      r          IS A `The readings of the forks in sections 88, 91, 125B and 125C`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`s 91 — the totals for an individual for` `the sale` `above the other taxable income` a `under the scale` bands `, reading the forks as` r MEANS
    concat (map (GIVEN m YIELD `the totals at m` m) (`s 91 — the material shareholder alternatives` (`s 91 — whether the seller is a material shareholder, for` `the sale` `, reading the forks as` r)))
    WHERE
        `the totals at m` MEANS
            GIVEN m YIELD
                `s 91 — the totals for an individual for` `the sale` `, a material shareholder:` m `, above the other taxable income` a `under the scale` bands `, reading the forks as` r

§§ `The tax on a sale`

-- (b2): an individual's gain on a unit in an oil or film partnership.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 91(b2) (source line 3361)
GIVEN `the sale` IS A `A sale for section 91`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 91(b2) — the individual's part taxed as in section 121 is more than nought for` `the sale` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the sale`'s `the seller`
    WHEN `an individual` `the records`   THEN `the sale`'s `the part of the real gain equal to depletion, exploration and development deductions or film production expenses on a unit in an oil or film partnership` GREATER THAN 0
    WHEN `a body of persons` `the rate`  THEN FALSE

-- The tax on a sale: (a) or (b)/(b1) with (c), then (f), then (g), the answer where every reading left open gives the same one.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 91 (source lines 3345-3391); forks S1, S2, S4, T1, T2, D2, V1, V2, V3; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVEN `the sale` IS A `A sale for section 91`
      a          IS A NUMBER
      bands      IS A LIST OF `A band of a marginal scale`
      r          IS A `The readings of the forks in sections 88, 91, 125B and 125C`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 91 — the tax on` `the sale` `, the seller's other taxable income being` a `under the scale` bands `, reading the forks as` r MEANS
    IF   `the sale`'s `the sale day` LESS THAN `s 88 — the change date`
    THEN `section 91 as deposited states the rates for a sale from the change date on`
    ELSE IF   `s 91(b2) — the individual's part taxed as in section 121 is more than nought for` `the sale`
         THEN `section 91(b2) for an individual leaves the place of the taxed part in the scale unsaid`
         ELSE CONSIDER `the common value of` `the totals`
              WHEN JUST v  THEN v
              WHEN NOTHING THEN `the tax turns on a reading that section 91 or section 88 leaves open`
    WHERE
        `the totals` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the sale`'s `the seller`
            WHEN `a body of persons` `the rate`  THEN `s 91 — the totals for a body of persons for` `the sale` `at the rate` `the rate` `, reading the forks as` r
            WHEN `an individual` `the records`   THEN `s 91 — the totals for an individual for` `the sale` `above the other taxable income` a `under the scale` bands `, reading the forks as` r

§§ `Paragraph (d): the report and the advance (not encoded)`

-- (d) requires the seller to report the sale to the assessing officer within 30 days of the sale on a form the Director sets, with the computation of the gain and the tax, and to pay an
-- advance of the tax; the officer may demand the report and the advance within 7 days, fix the original price, the consideration and the advance, and raise an advance he reasonably thinks
-- is 20% or more short; interest and linkage run from the 30 days; a securities sale with tax deducted at source is outside; the officer may extend, defer or reduce the advance.
-- NOT ENCODED: procedure and administration, not a rate (NOTES.md coverage table). The 30-day reporting day is the sale day plus 30 days; nothing else in (d) is a figure the rates need.
-- src:3363 | (ד)(1) נמכר נכס, יגיש המוכר לפקיד השומה, בתוך 30 ימים מיום המכירה, דוח בטופס שקבע המנהל, שיפרט את חישוב רווח ההון או הפסד ההון שהיה לו וחישוב המס החל במכירה כאמור, וישלם מקדמה בסכום המס החל על הרווח לפי סעיף זה.
-- src:3364 | (1א) [note: (החל ביום שיקבע שר האוצר בצו):] דוח כאמור בפסקה (1) יוגש במועד שנקבע באותה פסקה, באופן מקוון, בהתאם להוראות שקבע המנהל לפי סעיף 131ג(ד), והוראות סעיף 131ג יחולו.
-- src:3365 | (2) לא הוגש לפקיד השומה דוח כאמור בפסקה (1) או (1א), לפי העניין, ופקיד השומה סבור שאדם פלוני מכר נכס וחייב בתשלום מקדמה, רשאי הוא לדרוש הגשת הדוח ותשלום המקדמה בתוך 7 ימים מיום הדרישה, ואם לא נענה, רשאי הוא לקבוע את המחיר המקורי של הנכס הנמכר, את התמורה שהתקבלה ואת סכום המקדמה שבו חייב המוכר בשל רווח ההון; קבע פקיד השומה כאמור, תשולם המקדמה בתוך 7 ימים מיום שהומצאה הקביעה למוכר.
-- src:3366 | (2א) היה לפקיד השומה טעם סביר להניח כי המקדמה שעל המוכר לשלם על רווח ההון עולה ב־20% לפחות על סכום המקדמה שפורט בדוח שהוגש לפי הוראות פסקה (1), (1א) או (2), לפי העניין, רשאי הוא להגדיל את סכום המקדמה בגובה ההפרש הצפוי; קבע פקיד השומה כאמור, ישולם ההפרש בתוך 30 ימים מיום שניתנה החלטתו.
-- src:3367 | (2ב) דין החלטה כאמור בפסקאות (2) ו־(2א), לענין השגה וערעור, כדין שומה לפי סעיף 145(ב), ואולם השגה על החלטה לפי פסקה (2) תוגש רק בדרך של הגשת דוח כאמור בפסקה (1).
-- src:3368 | (2ג)(א) הוראות סעיף קטן זה לא יחולו על רווח הון במכירת נייר ערך הרשום למסחר בבורסה או במכירת יחידה, אם במועד המכירה נוכה מס מרווח ההון לפי סעיף 164.
-- src:3369 | (ב) לא נוכה המס כאמור בפסקת משנה (1) והמוכר חייב בהגשת דוח לפי סעיף 131, יוגש הדוח על רווח ההון, על אף האמור בפסקה (1) או (1א), לפי העניין, ביום 31 ביולי וביום 31 בינואר של כל שנת מס, בשל מכירה של ניירות ערך בששת החודשים שקדמו לחודש שבו חל יום הדיווח; עם הגשת הדוח כאמור, תשולם מקדמה בסכום המס החל לפי הוראות פקודה זו על רווח ההון בשל המכירה.
-- src:3370 | (ג) שר האוצר, באישור ועדת הכספים של הכנסת, רשאי לקבוע מקרים נוספים שלגביהם יחולו חובת דיווח ותשלום מקדמה כאמור בפסקה זו, הן לענין סוגי נכסים והן לענין סוגי נישומים, והכל בתיאומים, בתנאים ובשינויים שנקבעו.
-- src:3371 | (2ד) על אף האמור בפסקה (1) או (1א), לפי העניין, במכירת מניה בחבר־בני־אדם שהוחל בפירוקו כאמור בסעיף 93(א), יגיש המוכר, בתוך 30 ימים מיום שהוחל בפירוק, הודעה לפקיד השומה על תחילת הליכי הפירוק; העביר המפרק נכס לחבר באותו חבר־בני־אדם, כאמור באותו סעיף, ידווח החבר על רווח ההון שהיה לו, כאמור בסעיף קטן זה, בתוך 30 ימים מיום שהועבר אליו הנכס, וישלם מס בשיעורים הקבועים בסעיף זה, לפי הענין, משווי הנכס שהועבר כאמור; לענין פסקה זו, ”נכס“ – כהגדרתו בסעיף 93(ב6).
-- src:3372 | (2ה) פקיד השומה רשאי, אם ניתנה לו סיבה מספקת לכך, להאריך את המועד לתשלום המקדמה, וכן רשאי הוא לדחות את תשלום המס או להקטין את סכום המקדמה אם ראה שיש טעמים סבירים לכך שלא יחול מס על רווח ההון או שהמס שיחול יהיה בסכום אחר.
-- src:3373 | (3) לא שילם הנישום את המקדמה, כאמור בפסקאות (1) או (2) כולה או מקצתה, במועד, או ששילם מקדמה כאמור והתברר שהמס שהוא חייב בו עולה על המס ששילם, יהא חייב, מתום שלושים הימים האמורים ועד ליום התשלום:
-- src:3374 | (א) בתשלום הפרשי הצמדה וריבית כמשמעותם בסעיף 159א(א) על ההפרש שבין הסכום ששילם לבין סכום המס שהוא חייב בו;
-- src:3375 | (ב) [note: (נמחקה).]
-- src:3376 | (3א) חויב הנישום במקדמה לפי סעיף 48א לחוק מיסוי מקרקעין, או שנעשתה לו שומה עצמית או שומה סופית לפי אותו חוק, והתברר שהמס שהוא חייב בו עולה על המס שבו חויב לפי חוק מיסוי מקרקעין (להלן – הסכום לתשלום), יהא חייב, מתום התקופה הקבועה בחוק מיסוי מקרקעין, ועד ליום התשלום, בתשלום הפרשי הצמדה וריבית כמשמעותם בסעיף 159א(א), על ההפרש שבין הסכום לתשלום לבין המס שהוא חייב בו.
-- src:3377 | (4) מי שנתחייב בהפרשי הצמדה ובקנס לפי פסקה (3) לא יהיה חייב, לגבי אותם הסכומים והתקופות, בתשלומים האמורים בסעיפים 187 ו־190.
-- src:3378 | (5)(א) שילם הנישום מקדמה כאמור בפסקאות (1) או (2) או את סכום המס שהוא חייב בו לפי חוק מיסוי מקרקעין יתר על הסכום שהוא חייב בו על פי הדו״ח שהגיש לפי סעיף 131, תוחזר לו היתרה על פי הוראות סעיף 159א(ב) בתוספת הפרשי הצמדה וריבית כמשמעותם בסעיף 159א(א) לתקופה שמיום התשלום ועד ליום ההחזר.
-- src:3379 | (ב) הוראות סעיף 159א(ג) ו־(ד) וסעיף 160 לא יחולו על החזר כאמור בפסקת משנה (א).
-- src:3380 | (6) סכום שנוכה לפי סעיפים 93(ב4), 164 ו־170 בשל רווח ההון, יראוהו כתשלום על חשבון המקדמה שהנישום חייב בה והוא יהיה זכאי לקזזו מהמקדמה, ובלבד שיש בידו אישור בכתב בדבר הניכוי; ואולם קיזוז כנגד המס שחייב בו בעל מניות מהותי ייעשה רק לאחר שהסכום שנוכה שולם לפקיד השומה, זולת אם בעל המניות המהותי מחזיק בסוג כלשהו של אמצעי השליטה בשיעור נמוך מ־50%, והוא הוכיח להנחת דעתו של פקיד השומה שלא ידע כי הסכום שנוכה לא שולם לפקיד השומה או שנקט בכל האמצעים הסבירים להבטחת התשלום.

§§ `Paragraph (h): the Minister's power for transfers between controlling shareholders (not encoded)`

-- (h) lets the Minister of Finance, with the approval of the Finance Committee, fix that for special events or circumstances in which assets are transferred between controlling shareholders or
-- connected parties the rates of ss 121 or 126 apply notwithstanding s 91. A power, no rule; no order is deposited (NOTES.md coverage table).
-- src:3390 | (ח) שר האוצר, באישור ועדת הכספים של הכנסת, רשאי לקבוע כי לענין אירועים מיוחדים או נסיבות מיוחדות שבהן הועברו נכסים בין בעלי שליטה או צדדים קשורים, יחולו, על אף הוראות סעיף זה, שיעורי המס כאמור בסעיפים 121 או 126, לפי הענין.
-- src:3391 | [note: פורסמו תקנות מס הכנסה (שיעורי מס מיוחדים לענין מי שהחזיק בנייר ערך זר לפני יום רישומו למסחר בבורסה מחוץ לישראל), התשס״ד–2004.]

§§ `Paragraph (e): spreading the real gain over up to four tax years`

-- src:3381 | (ה)(1) לפי בקשת הנישום יחושב המס על ריווח ההון הריאלי כאילו נבע הריווח בחלקים שנתיים שווים תוך תקופה שאינה עולה על ארבע שנות מס או על תקופת הבעלות בנכס, לפי הקצרה שבהן והמסתיימת בשנת המס שבה נבע הריווח; ואולם לענין קביעת המקדמות לפי סעיפים 174 עד 181 יראו את ההכנסה בכל אחת מהשנים האמורות שבתוך התקופה האמורה, כאילו הוסף עליה החלק השנתי; חישוב המס ייעשה בהתחשב בשיעור המס הקבוע בסעיף קטן (ב), ולענין מס שבח – בהתחשב בשיעור המס הקבוע בסעיף 48א(ב) לחוק מיסוי מקרקעין, וכן בהתחשב בשיעורי המס החלים על כלל הכנסתו החייבת של הנישום וביתרת נקודות הזיכוי שזכאי להן הנישום בכל אחת משנות המס בתקופה האמורה; לענין סעיף קטן זה, ”תקופת הבעלות בנכס“ – תקופה שתחילתה בתחילת שנת המס שלאחר שנת המס שבה הגיע הנכס לידי הנישום וסיומה בתום שנת המס שבה יצא הנכס מידיו.
-- src:3382 | (2) במכירת נכס שיום רכישתו לפני המועד הקובע או במכירת זכות במקרקעין או בפעולה באיגוד מקרקעין, כשיום הרכישה של הזכות במקרקעין או הזכות באיגוד המקרקעין לפי הענין, היה לפני יום התחילה, יחולו הוראות פסקה (1) בשינויים אלה:
-- src:3383 | (א) רווח ההון הריאלי עד המועד הקובע רווח ההון הריאלי לאחר המועד הקובע ועד למועד השינוי, יתרת רווח ההון הריאלי לאחר מועד השינוי, השבח הריאלי עד יום התחילה, השבח הריאלי לאחר יום התחילה ועד למועד השינוי ויתרת השבח הריאלי לאחר מועד השינוי, לפי הענין, יחושבו כפי שהיו מחושבים אילולא הגיש הנישום בקשה כאמור בפסקה (1);
-- src:3384 | (ב) חישוב המס ייעשה בהתחשב בשיעורי המס הקבועים בסעיף קטן (ב1) או בסעיף 48א(ב1) לחוק מיסוי מקרקעין, לפי הענין, וכן בהתחשב בשיעורי המס החלים על כלל הכנסתו החייבת של הנישום וביתרת נקודות הזיכוי שלהן הוא זכאי, כאמור בפסקה (1);
-- src:3385 | (ג) בסעיף קטן זה, ”זכות במקרקעין“, ”זכות באיגוד מקרקעין“, ”יום התחילה“, ”מס שבח“, ”שבח ריאלי עד יום התחילה“, ”יתרת השבח הריאלי לאחר יום התחילה ועד למועד השינוי“ ו”יתרת השבח הריאלי לאחר מועד השינוי“ – כהגדרתם בחוק מיסוי מקרקעין.
-- src:3386 | (3) הוראות פסקה (1) לא יחולו על רווח הון במכירת ניירות ערך הרשומים למסחר בבורסה.

GIVETH A NUMBER
`section 91(e)(3) does not let the gain on a security registered for trading on a stock exchange be spread` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 91(e)(3) does not apply paragraph (1), spreading, to a gain on a security registered for trading on a stock exchange"

GIVETH A NUMBER
`this model does not combine the spreading of section 91(e) with paragraph (f), (g) or (b2)` MEANS
    REFUSE "this model does not combine the spreading of section 91(e) with paragraph (f), (g) or (b2): the text does not say how the caps and the halving fall on the years"

GIVETH A NUMBER
`section 91(e) spreads the tax of paragraph (b), which is an individual's` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 91(e) spreads the tax computed at the rates of paragraph (b), which is an individual's, so it is not open to a body of persons"

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the period of ownership gives no tax year over which to spread` MEANS
    REFUSE "the period of ownership of section 91(e)(1) begins with the tax year after the year the asset reached the taxpayer, and here it gives no tax year"

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the years given are not the years of the period` MEANS
    REFUSE "the number of tax years given is not the number of years over which section 91(e)(1) spreads the gain"

-- The number of tax years: the shorter of four and the period of ownership, which starts at the start of the tax year after the year the asset reached
-- the taxpayer and ends at the end of the tax year in which it left his hands (the year of the sale).
-- (0.1.1) For a right sold in the year it reached the seller the period is empty, and the text does not say what "the shorter of four years and the period" is: fork T3.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the text does not say whether an empty period of ownership gives no tax year or one` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 91(e)(1) spreads over the shorter of four tax years and the period of ownership, and for a right sold in the year it reached the seller the period is empty; the text does not say whether that gives no tax year or one"

@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 91(e)(1) (source line 3381); fork T3
GIVEN `the sale` IS A `A sale for section 91`
      e          IS A `A reading of a period of ownership that is empty`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 91(e)(1) — the number of tax years for` `the sale` `, reading an empty period as` e MEANS
    IF   `the full years` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN min 4 `the full years`
    ELSE CONSIDER e
         WHEN `an empty period gives no tax year`                          THEN 0
         WHEN `an empty period gives one tax year`                         THEN 1
         WHEN `declined where an empty period changes the answer`          THEN `the text does not say whether an empty period of ownership gives no tax year or one`
    WHERE
        `the full years` MEANS DATE_YEAR (`the sale`'s `the sale day`) MINUS `the sale`'s `the tax year in which the asset reached the seller`

GIVEN `the sale` IS A `A sale for section 91`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 91(e)(1) — the number of tax years for` `the sale` MEANS
    `s 91(e)(1) — the number of tax years for` `the sale` `, reading an empty period as` `declined where an empty period changes the answer`

-- The three parts of the real gain of (b1), by the readings named: the same parts that `s 91(b1) — the tax of an individual` taxes.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 91(b1)(1)-(1A) (source lines 3352-3358); s 88 (lines 3311-3314); forks S2, V3
GIVEN `the sale` IS A `A sale for section 91`
      c          IS A `A reading of how the days of a period are counted`
      v          IS A `A reading of the real gain used for the middle part of a security bought before the fixed date`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`s 91(b1) — the three parts of the real gain of` `the sale` `, counting the days as` c `, reading the middle part as` v MEANS
    LIST `the first part`, `the middle part`, `the last part`
    WHERE
        `the gain` MEANS `s 91 — the real capital gain to be taxed, of` `the sale`
        `the reduction applies` MEANS
                `the sale`'s `the asset is a security`
            AND `the sale`'s `the purchase day` LESS THAN `s 88 — the fixed date`
            AND `the sale`'s `the distributable profits of section 94B deducted for a security bought before the fixed date` GREATER THAN 0
        `the reduced gain` MEANS max 0 (`the gain` MINUS `the sale`'s `the distributable profits of section 94B deducted for a security bought before the fixed date`)
        `the gain for the first and the last part` MEANS IF `the reduction applies` THEN `the reduced gain` ELSE `the gain`
        `the gain for the middle part` MEANS
            IF `the reduction applies`
            THEN CONSIDER v
                 WHEN `the gain reduced by the distributable profits is used for all three parts`  THEN `the reduced gain`
                 WHEN `the gain before the reduction is used for the middle part`                  THEN `the gain`
                 WHEN `declined where the real gain used for the middle part changes the answer`   THEN `the reduced gain`
            ELSE `the gain`
        `the first part` MEANS
            `s 88 — the real capital gain up to the fixed date, of` `the gain for the first and the last part` `bought on` (`the sale`'s `the purchase day`) `and sold on` (`the sale`'s `the sale day`) `, counting the days as` c
        `the middle part` MEANS
            `s 88 — the real capital gain after the fixed date up to the change date, of` `the gain for the middle part` `bought on` (`the sale`'s `the purchase day`) `and sold on` (`the sale`'s `the sale day`) `, counting the days as` c
        `the last part` MEANS `the gain for the first and the last part` MINUS `the first part` MINUS `the middle part`

-- One year of spreading under (b): the year's share of the gain as a layer above that year's other income, less the credit points left unused.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 91(e)(1) (source line 3381); fork T1
GIVEN `the sale`  IS A `A sale for section 91`
      n           IS A NUMBER
      m           IS A BOOLEAN
      t           IS A `A reading of a cap on the rate where the gain stands in several bands`
      `the year`  IS A `A tax year in the period of spreading`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 91(e)(1) — the tax of one year of` `the sale` `spread over` n `years, a material shareholder:` m `, applying the cap as` t `, the year being` `the year` MEANS
    max 0 (`the tax on a layer of` (`s 91 — the real capital gain to be taxed, of` `the sale` DIVIDED BY n) `standing on the other taxable income` (`the year`'s `the other taxable income that year`) `under the scale` (`the year`'s `the scale of section 121 for that year`) `with the rate capped at` (`s 91(b) — the highest rate for` (`the sale`'s `the kind of asset sold`) `when the seller is a material shareholder:` m) `, applying the cap as` t
           MINUS `the year`'s `the value of the credit points left unused that year`)

-- One year of spreading under (e)(2): each of the three parts of (b1), divided by the number of years, above that year's other income, less the unused credit points.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 91(e)(2) (source lines 3382-3385); s 91(b1); forks S2, T1, T2, V3
GIVEN `the sale`  IS A `A sale for section 91`
      n           IS A NUMBER
      m           IS A BOOLEAN
      c           IS A `A reading of how the days of a period are counted`
      t           IS A `A reading of a cap on the rate where the gain stands in several bands`
      o           IS A `A reading of where each part of a gain stands in the top layer`
      v           IS A `A reading of the real gain used for the middle part of a security bought before the fixed date`
      `the year`  IS A `A tax year in the period of spreading`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 91(e)(2) — the tax of one year of` `the sale` `spread over` n `years, a material shareholder:` m `, counting the days as` c `, applying the cap as` t `, placing the parts as` o `, reading the middle part as` v `, the year being` `the year` MEANS
    max 0 (`the tax of three parts` (`the part` 0 DIVIDED BY n) `and` (`the part` 1 DIVIDED BY n) `and` (`the part` 2 DIVIDED BY n) `capped at` `these rates are percentages, and nothing in the scale exceeds a hundred percent` `and` (`s 91(b1) — the highest rate for the middle period for` (`the sale`'s `the kind of asset sold`) `when the seller is a material shareholder:` m) `and` (`s 91(b) — the highest rate for` (`the sale`'s `the kind of asset sold`) `when the seller is a material shareholder:` m) `above the other taxable income` (`the year`'s `the other taxable income that year`) `under the scale` (`the year`'s `the scale of section 121 for that year`) `, applying the cap as` t `, with the parts placed as` o
           MINUS `the year`'s `the value of the credit points left unused that year`)
    WHERE
        `the part` MEANS GIVEN k YIELD at (`s 91(b1) — the three parts of the real gain of` `the sale` `, counting the days as` c `, reading the middle part as` v) k

-- (e)(1) over the readings of the cap: one total for each, with (c) added (the chargeable inflationary amount is not spread).
GIVEN `the sale`  IS A `A sale for section 91`
      `the years` IS A LIST OF `A tax year in the period of spreading`
      m           IS A BOOLEAN
      r           IS A `The readings of the forks in sections 88, 91, 125B and 125C`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`s 91(e)(1) — the totals for` `the sale` `over` `the years` `, a material shareholder:` m `, reading the forks as` r MEANS
    map (GIVEN t YIELD `the total at t` t) (`the explicit readings of the cap in` (r's `a cap where the gain stands in several bands`))
    WHERE
        `the total at t` MEANS
            GIVEN t YIELD
                sum (map (GIVEN y YIELD `s 91(e)(1) — the tax of one year of` `the sale` `spread over` (`s 91(e)(1) — the number of tax years for` `the sale`) `years, a material shareholder:` m `, applying the cap as` t `, the year being` y) `the years`)
                PLUS `s 91(c) — the tax on the chargeable inflationary amount of` `the sale`

-- (e)(2): the innermost reading, V3.
GIVEN `the sale`  IS A `A sale for section 91`
      `the years` IS A LIST OF `A tax year in the period of spreading`
      m           IS A BOOLEAN
      c           IS A `A reading of how the days of a period are counted`
      t           IS A `A reading of a cap on the rate where the gain stands in several bands`
      o           IS A `A reading of where each part of a gain stands in the top layer`
      r           IS A `The readings of the forks in sections 88, 91, 125B and 125C`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`s 91(e)(2) — the totals for` `the sale` `over` `the years` `, a material shareholder:` m `, days counted as` c `, cap applied as` t `, parts placed as` o `, reading the forks as` r MEANS
    map (GIVEN v YIELD `the total at v` v) (`s 91(b1) — the explicit readings of the middle part in` (r's `the real gain for the middle part`))
    WHERE
        `the total at v` MEANS
            GIVEN v YIELD
                sum (map (GIVEN y YIELD `s 91(e)(2) — the tax of one year of` `the sale` `spread over` (`s 91(e)(1) — the number of tax years for` `the sale`) `years, a material shareholder:` m `, counting the days as` c `, applying the cap as` t `, placing the parts as` o `, reading the middle part as` v `, the year being` y) `the years`)
                PLUS `s 91(c) — the tax on the chargeable inflationary amount of` `the sale`

GIVEN `the sale`  IS A `A sale for section 91`
      `the years` IS A LIST OF `A tax year in the period of spreading`
      m           IS A BOOLEAN
      c           IS A `A reading of how the days of a period are counted`
      t           IS A `A reading of a cap on the rate where the gain stands in several bands`
      r           IS A `The readings of the forks in sections 88, 91, 125B and 125C`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`s 91(e)(2) — the totals for` `the sale` `over` `the years` `, a material shareholder:` m `, days counted as` c `, cap applied as` t `, reading the forks as` r MEANS
    concat (map (GIVEN o YIELD `the totals at o` o) (`the explicit readings of where the parts stand in` (r's `where each part stands in the top layer`)))
    WHERE
        `the totals at o` MEANS
            GIVEN o YIELD
                `s 91(e)(2) — the totals for` `the sale` `over` `the years` `, a material shareholder:` m `, days counted as` c `, cap applied as` t `, parts placed as` o `, reading the forks as` r

GIVEN `the sale`  IS A `A sale for section 91`
      `the years` IS A LIST OF `A tax year in the period of spreading`
      m           IS A BOOLEAN
      c           IS A `A reading of how the days of a period are counted`
      r           IS A `The readings of the forks in sections 88, 91, 125B and 125C`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`s 91(e)(2) — the totals for` `the sale` `over` `the years` `, a material shareholder:` m `, days counted as` c `, reading the forks as` r MEANS
    concat (map (GIVEN t YIELD `the totals at t` t) (`the explicit readings of the cap in` (r's `a cap where the gain stands in several bands`)))
    WHERE
        `the totals at t` MEANS
            GIVEN t YIELD
                `s 91(e)(2) — the totals for` `the sale` `over` `the years` `, a material shareholder:` m `, days counted as` c `, cap applied as` t `, reading the forks as` r

GIVEN `the sale`  IS A `A sale for section 91`
      `the years` IS A LIST OF `A tax year in the period of spreading`
      m           IS A BOOLEAN
      r           IS A `The readings of the forks in sections 88, 91, 125B and 125C`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`s 91(e)(2) — the totals for` `the sale` `over` `the years` `, a material shareholder:` m `, reading the forks as` r MEANS
    concat (map (GIVEN c YIELD `the totals at c` c) (`s 88 — the explicit readings of the day count in` (r's `counting the days of a period`)))
    WHERE
        `the totals at c` MEANS
            GIVEN c YIELD
                `s 91(e)(2) — the totals for` `the sale` `over` `the years` `, a material shareholder:` m `, days counted as` c `, reading the forks as` r

-- Whether (f), (g) or (b2) reaches the sale: the spreading is not combined with them in this model.
GIVEN `the sale` IS A `A sale for section 91`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 91(e) — paragraph (f), (g) or (b2) reaches` `the sale` MEANS
        `the sale`'s `the asset was expropriated`
     OR `the sale`'s `the tax year in which the asset reached the seller` AT MOST 1960
     OR `the sale`'s `the part of the real gain equal to depletion, exploration and development deductions or film production expenses on a unit in an oil or film partnership` GREATER THAN 0

-- The tax on a sale spread over its years at the taxpayer's request: the answer where every reading left open gives the same one.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 91(e) (source lines 3381-3386); forks S1, S2, S4, T1, T2, D2, V3; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVEN `the sale`  IS A `A sale for section 91`
      `the years` IS A LIST OF `A tax year in the period of spreading`
      r           IS A `The readings of the forks in sections 88, 91, 125B and 125C`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 91(e) — the tax over the years given, the number of them being fixed, on` `the sale` `spread over the years` `the years` `, reading the forks as` r MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the sale`'s `the sale day` LESS THAN `s 88 — the change date`
            THEN `section 91 as deposited states the rates for a sale from the change date on`
        IF `the seller is a body of persons`
            THEN `section 91(e) spreads the tax of paragraph (b), which is an individual's`
        IF `the sale`'s `registered for trading on a stock exchange`
            THEN `section 91(e)(3) does not let the gain on a security registered for trading on a stock exchange be spread`
        IF `s 91(e) — paragraph (f), (g) or (b2) reaches` `the sale`
            THEN `this model does not combine the spreading of section 91(e) with paragraph (f), (g) or (b2)`
        IF `s 91(e)(1) — the number of tax years for` `the sale` LESS THAN 1
            THEN `the period of ownership gives no tax year over which to spread`
        IF NOT (count `the years` EQUALS `s 91(e)(1) — the number of tax years for` `the sale`)
            THEN `the years given are not the years of the period`
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `the common value of` `the totals`
            WHEN JUST v  THEN v
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `the tax turns on a reading that section 91 or section 88 leaves open`
    WHERE
        `the seller is a body of persons` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the sale`'s `the seller`
            WHEN `an individual` `the records`   THEN FALSE
            WHEN `a body of persons` `the rate`  THEN TRUE
        `the totals` MEANS
            concat (map (GIVEN m YIELD `the totals for m` m) (`s 91 — the material shareholder alternatives` (`s 91 — whether the seller is a material shareholder, for` `the sale` `, reading the forks as` r)))
        `the totals for m` MEANS
            GIVEN m YIELD
                IF   `s 91(b1) — the layered rates apply to` `the sale`
                THEN `s 91(e)(2) — the totals for` `the sale` `over` `the years` `, a material shareholder:` m `, reading the forks as` r
                ELSE `s 91(e)(1) — the totals for` `the sale` `over` `the years` `, a material shareholder:` m `, reading the forks as` r

-- The sale as if the right had reached the seller in the year before the year of the sale: an empty period read as one tax year (fork T3).
GIVEN `the sale` IS A `A sale for section 91`
GIVETH A `A sale for section 91`
`the sale with an empty period read as one tax year:` `the sale` MEANS
    `A sale for section 91` WITH
        `the seller`                                                         IS `the sale`'s `the seller`
        `the kind of asset sold`                                             IS `the sale`'s `the kind of asset sold`
        `registered for trading on a stock exchange`                         IS `the sale`'s `registered for trading on a stock exchange`
        `registered for trading on a stock exchange before the change date`  IS `the sale`'s `registered for trading on a stock exchange before the change date`
        `a unit in an exempt mutual fund`                                    IS `the sale`'s `a unit in an exempt mutual fund`
        `the real capital gain`                                              IS `the sale`'s `the real capital gain`
        `the capital gain`                                                   IS `the sale`'s `the capital gain`
        `the chargeable inflationary amount`                                 IS `the sale`'s `the chargeable inflationary amount`
        `the purchase day`                                                   IS `the sale`'s `the purchase day`
        `the sale day`                                                       IS `the sale`'s `the sale day`
        `the asset is a security`                                            IS `the sale`'s `the asset is a security`
        `the distributable profits of section 94B deducted for a security bought before the fixed date` IS `the sale`'s `the distributable profits of section 94B deducted for a security bought before the fixed date`
        `the asset was expropriated`                                         IS `the sale`'s `the asset was expropriated`
        `the tax year in which the asset reached the seller`                 IS DATE_YEAR (`the sale`'s `the sale day`) MINUS 1
        `the part of the real gain equal to depletion, exploration and development deductions or film production expenses on a unit in an oil or film partnership` IS `the sale`'s `the part of the real gain equal to depletion, exploration and development deductions or film production expenses on a unit in an oil or film partnership`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`section 91(e) with an empty period of ownership and the years given` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 91(e)(1) spreads over the shorter of four tax years and the period of ownership, and for a right sold in the year it reached the seller the period is empty; the text does not say whether that gives no tax year or one, and here it changes the answer"

-- The tax on a sale spread over its years at the taxpayer's request, the answer where every reading left open gives the same one, with fork T3 named.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 91(e)(1) (source line 3381); fork T3; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVEN `the sale`  IS A `A sale for section 91`
      `the years` IS A LIST OF `A tax year in the period of spreading`
      r           IS A `The readings of the forks in sections 88, 91, 125B and 125C`
      e           IS A `A reading of a period of ownership that is empty`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 91(e) — the tax on` `the sale` `spread over the years` `the years` `, reading the forks as` r `and an empty period as` e MEANS
    IF   DATE_YEAR (`the sale`'s `the sale day`) MINUS `the sale`'s `the tax year in which the asset reached the seller` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `s 91(e) — the tax over the years given, the number of them being fixed, on` `the sale` `spread over the years` `the years` `, reading the forks as` r
    ELSE CONSIDER e
         WHEN `an empty period gives no tax year`
           THEN `the period of ownership gives no tax year over which to spread`
         WHEN `an empty period gives one tax year`
           THEN `s 91(e) — the tax over the years given, the number of them being fixed, on` (`the sale with an empty period read as one tax year:` `the sale`) `spread over the years` `the years` `, reading the forks as` r
         WHEN `declined where an empty period changes the answer`
           THEN `section 91(e) with an empty period of ownership and the years given`

-- The tax on a sale spread over its years: an empty period of ownership is declined by default.
GIVEN `the sale`  IS A `A sale for section 91`
      `the years` IS A LIST OF `A tax year in the period of spreading`
      r           IS A `The readings of the forks in sections 88, 91, 125B and 125C`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 91(e) — the tax on` `the sale` `spread over the years` `the years` `, reading the forks as` r MEANS
    `s 91(e) — the tax on` `the sale` `spread over the years` `the years` `, reading the forks as` r `and an empty period as` `declined where an empty period changes the answer`
